  "label": "Transcriptomic Signature Integration Methods",
  "related": [
    "integrative-identification-14c8",
    "fetal-maternal-d0f2",
    "tumor-glioblastoma-efcd"
  ],
  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "variant-risk-2502",
  "summary": "Public single-cell, spatial, and bulk datasets are being reanalyzed with donor-aware and cross-platform designs to test signature robustness.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is reanalysis of public data under explicit robustness controls. Donor-aware designs appear in meniscus and aortic valve scRNA-seq and spatial studies, while cross-pipeline and cross-platform checks appear in colorectal and breast cancer signatures. The breast cancer study reports 666 consistently upregulated genes, with 93% validating in full TCGA-BRCA. A tumor-budding signature (AIF1, LIF, MRC1, TNC) is evaluated across platforms. A Tetralogy of Fallot meta-analysis reports its endothelial M1 module as the strongest signal. Methodologically, CellDEEP uses metacells to reduce false positives relative to single-cell methods, CDGE separates direct from mediated differential expression, and rpMeta integrates paired RNA-seq and proteomics for higher sensitivity. Several items report null or hypothesis-generating outcomes, including the meniscus MSC-EV analysis, where no enrichment survived multiplicity correction.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-21"
}
